hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1443","‘A’ishah Siddiqah, Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her), says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would fall ill, Jibril (peace be upon him) would recite this supplication over him: “In the name of Allah, I seek help for you. May He cure you from every illness, protect you from the evil of every envious person, and safeguard you from the harm of every evil eye.”"
"1444","'Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib narrates from Abu Nadrah, and he from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) that Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Muhammad (peace be upon you)! Have you fallen ill?"" He (peace be upon him) replied, ""Yes."" Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) said, ""I perform ruqyah on you in the name of Allah from everything that troubles you, and from the evil of every soul or envious eye. May Allah grant you healing. In the name of Allah, I perform ruqyah on you."""
"1445","‘Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that a Jew from Banu Zurayq, Labeed bin A’sam, cast magic on the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), to the extent that the Prophet (peace be upon him) would imagine that he was doing something, even though he had not done it. One day or one night, the Prophet (peace be upon him) made supplication, then made supplication again, then said, “O Aisha! Do you know that Allah, the Glorious and Majestic, has informed me of what I asked Him?” Two men came to me, one sat at my head and the other at my feet (they were both angels). The one sitting at my head said to the one at my feet, and the one at my feet said to the one at my head, “What is wrong with this man?” He replied, “He has been affected by magic.” He asked, “Who has done magic on him?” He replied, “Labeed bin A’sam.” Then he asked, “In what has the magic been done?” He replied, “In a comb and the hair that falls from it, and in the fibers of a male date palm’s spadix.” He asked, “Where is it kept?” He replied, “In the well of Dhi Arwan.” Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went to that well with some of his companions, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said, “O Aisha! By Allah, the water of this well was as if it were the infusion of henna, and the date palms there were as if they were the heads of devils.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! Why did you not burn it?” (meaning the hair and other things that were taken out) The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, “Allah has cured me, and I disliked stirring up trouble among the people, so I ordered it to be buried.”"
"1446","‘Umm al-Mu’minin A’ishah Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when there was someone ill in the house, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would recite the Mu’awwidhat (Surah al-Falaq and Surah an-Naas) and blow over him. Then, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) himself fell ill, in the illness during which he passed away, I would blow over him and would pass his own hand over him, because his blessed hand had more blessing than my hand."
"1447","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Uthman bin Abi al-As Thaqafi (may Allah be pleased with him) that he complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about a pain that had developed in his body since he became Muslim. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Place your hand on the place of pain and say 'Bismillah' three times, then say this seven times: 'I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of what I find and from the evil of what I fear.'"""
"1448","´It is narrated from Abu’l-‘Ala: Sayyiduna ‘Uthman bin Abu’l-‘As (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! Satan comes between me and my prayer and makes me forget the Qur’an.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “That Satan is called Khanzab. When you feel his effect, seek refuge with Allah from him and spit lightly to your left three times (during the prayer).” Sayyiduna ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “I did that, and Allah removed that Satan from me.”"
"1449","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) were on a journey and passed by a tribe of the Arabs. They asked them for hospitality, but they did not offer them any hospitality. Then they (the people of the tribe) said, ""Is there anyone among you who knows incantation (ruqyah)?"" Their chief had been stung by a scorpion. One of the companions said, ""Yes, I know an incantation."" Then he recited Surah Al-Fatihah and blew over him, and he was cured. So they gave them a flock of sheep, but they did not accept it and said, ""I will ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" Then they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and related the incident and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! By Allah, I did nothing except recite Surah Al-Fatihah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled and said, ""How did you know that it is an incantation?"" Then he said, ""Take the flock of sheep and allocate a share for me as well (because the Qur'an was revealed to the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"1450","Aswad says: I asked Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) about ruqyah (spiritual healing), so she said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had permitted the people of one house among the Ansar to perform ruqyah for poison (such as from snake or scorpion bites)."
"1451","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says` The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted ruqyah (spiritual healing) for the evil eye, stings (poison), and namlah. (Namlah is a boil that causes burning and changes its place, or those boils that appear in the armpit.)"
"1452","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade incantations (ruqyah). Then the people of Amr bin Hazm came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We have an incantation for scorpion stings, but you have forbidden incantations?"" The narrator says that they presented that incantation before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: ""I do not see any harm in it. If any of you can benefit his brother, then let him do so."""
"1453","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I suffered greatly from a scorpion that stung me last night."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If you had said in the evening: (('I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created')), it would not have harmed you (it would not have stung you)."""
"1454","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The evil eye is real (that is, it has an effect by the command of Allah Almighty), and if anything could overtake destiny, it would be the evil eye (but nothing can overtake destiny). When you are asked to perform ghusl (ritual washing), then perform ghusl. (Because if someone is afflicted by the evil eye, and the person who cast the evil eye performs ghusl and its water is used to wash the afflicted person, then he is cured.)"""
"1455","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to instruct me to perform ruqyah (spiritual healing) because of the evil eye."
"1456","‘Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted the people of Al-Hazm to perform ruqyah (incantation) for snake bites. And he said to Asma bint Umais (may Allah be pleased with her): “What is the reason that I find my brother’s children (i.e., the sons of Ja’far bin Abi Talib) thin? Are they hungry?” Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “No, they are quickly affected by the evil eye.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Perform ruqyah for them.” I presented a ruqyah before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: “Recite this ruqyah over them.”"
"1457","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a girl in the house of Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), who had freckles on her face (that is, she had jaundice, her face was yellowish), and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""She has been affected by the evil eye, perform ruqyah for her."""
"1458","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her): When any of us would fall ill or suffer a wound, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would place his index finger on the ground and say, ""In the name of Allah, the soil of our land, with the saliva of one of us, so that our sick may be cured by the permission of Allah, the Exalted."""
"1459","Sayyidah Khawlah bint Hakim al-Salamiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever stops at any place and then says, ""I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,"" nothing will harm him until he departs from that place."
"1460","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when any of us would fall ill, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would pass his right hand over them, then say: “O Master, remove this illness and grant health, You are the Giver of healing, Your healing alone is true, grant such a healing that no illness remains.” When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) himself fell ill and his illness became severe, I took his hand to do as he used to do (that is, I intended to pass his hand and recite this supplication), but he withdrew his hand from my hand and then said: “O Allah! Forgive me and join me with the Highest Companion.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that then when I looked, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had passed away. (That is, with this supplication, Allah the Exalted called him to Himself.)"
"1461","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite this supplication: ""O Master! Remove this illness. Healing is in Your hand alone; there is no one who can remove it except You."""
"1462","Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik Ashja'i (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We used to perform ruqyah (incantations) during the time of ignorance. We said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What do you say about this?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Present your ruqyah to me. There is nothing wrong with ruqyah as long as it does not contain anything of shirk (associating partners with Allah)."""
